# ── Dependencies / build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Native build artifacts (Capacitor/Android). APKs are generated, never source.
*.apk
*.aab

# ── Large local-only data (NEVER commit these) ───────────────────────────────
# GitHub hard-rejects files over 100 MB. sqlite-latest.sqlite is ~553 MB.
# It's the raw EVE static data dump used by scripts/update-from-evedb.py to
# regenerate the dogma bundles. Each dev downloads it themselves; it is not
# a source file.
sqlite-latest.sqlite
*.sqlite
*.db

# The pyfa checkout (icons + eve.db). App.jsx globs icons from here, but
# eveIcon() falls back to CCP's image server when the glob is empty, so the
# app works fine without it. Keeping it out of the repo saves a huge checkout.
# It is ALSO what the oracle runs eos from, so it must match eve.db's version —
# eos_bootstrap refuses to run otherwise. There is deliberately only ONE clone:
# a second, older one was the single biggest source of false "pyfa doesn't
# implement this" conclusions.
Pyfa-master/
pyfa-master/
*.zip

# ── Oracle: personal pyfa fit dumps (OPSEC — NEVER commit) ────────────────────
# scripts/oracle/*.py and *.mjs are tooling and SHOULD be committed, but the
# scanned/exported fit dumps contain the user's real fits, some OPSEC-sensitive.
# The leading underscore is the convention for "working data, not tooling", so ignore it
# whatever the extension — the sweeps also drop .log and .txt scratch beside the .jsonl.
scripts/oracle/_*
scripts/oracle/*.err
scripts/oracle/__pycache__/

# ── Generated native iOS project ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unlike android/, ios/ is NOT committed. The TestFlight workflow regenerates it with
# `npx cap add ios` on every run, so a stale native project can never drift from the web
# code, and the ~thousands of CocoaPods files stay out of the repo. Everything that would
# otherwise be hand-edited in Xcode lives in scripts/patch-ios-project.sh instead.
ios/

# ── Signing material (NEVER commit — this repo is public) ────────────────────
# The iOS distribution private key, its .p12 bundle, the App Store Connect API key and
# provisioning profiles. These belong in GitHub Actions secrets (see IOS_RELEASE.md) and
# nowhere else. Keep the working copies outside the repo entirely; this is a backstop.
*.key
*.p12
*.pem
*.csr
*.cer
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore
*.jks
# The Android upload keystore's path and its three passwords, in plaintext. Read by
# android/app/build.gradle; see "Google Play" under Shipping a release in CLAUDE.md for setup.
key.properties

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node
